From e9d1afb69845efde65f09cbbe415fd0eafe22ed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 14:14:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bsps/riscv/mbv: Shut the board down through a test finisher

bsp_reset() used bspreset-loop.c, which spins.  On real hardware that is
all it can do, but under QEMU it leaves the simulator running after the
system has halted.  An automated test runner then cannot tell a test which
failed and shut down from one which hung -- rtems-test reports both as a
timeout -- and every test costs the runner's full timeout however quickly
it finishes.  A full test suite run is impractical as a result.

Look for a SiFive test finisher in the device tree and write the finisher
value to it, falling back to spinning when there is none, so real hardware
is unaffected.  The device tree gains the node QEMU's
amd-microblaze-v-generic machine needs; note the machine only grew such a
device recently, and the BSP has to be given the device tree through
MBV_FDT_PROBE_ADDRESS because that machine hands over none of its own.

With all of it in place hello.exe goes from occupying the runner for its
full timeout to exiting in 74ms, and dl06 and ttest01 now terminate in
under 100ms while still reporting their failures.  A 674 test sweep takes
5m44s.  No test verdict changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../mbv/dts/amd-microblaze-v-generic.dts      |  5 ++
 bsps/riscv/mbv/start/bspreset.c               | 79 +++++++++++++++++++
 spec/build/bsps/riscv/mbv/obj.yml             |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 bsps/riscv/mbv/start/bspreset.c

diff --git a/bsps/riscv/mbv/dts/amd-microblaze-v-generic.dts b/bsps/riscv/mbv/dts/amd-microblaze-v-generic.dts
index 495652b28b..7b20b64162 100644
--- a/bsps/riscv/mbv/dts/amd-microblaze-v-generic.dts
+++ b/bsps/riscv/mbv/dts/amd-microblaze-v-generic.dts
@@ -173,4 +173,9 @@
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x80000000 0x10000000>;
 	};
+
+	test@40100000 {
+		compatible = "sifive,test1", "sifive,test0", "syscon";
+		reg = <0x40100000 0x1000>;
+	};
 };
diff --git a/bsps/riscv/mbv/start/bspreset.c b/bsps/riscv/mbv/start/bspreset.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..4f83bb0dd4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bsps/riscv/mbv/start/bspreset.c
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
